    "body": "## Pull Request Overview\n\nThis PR defines the SPDM (Security Protocol and Data Model) data structure and flows for the CoVE-IO specification. It introduces mechanisms for passing SPDM metadata between the TSM and host security domain manager during device connections.\n\nKey changes:\n- Added SPDM data structure definition with certificate chains and measurements\n- Extended connect_device function to include SPDM data output parameters\n- Added new sbi_covh_spdm_data function for passing SPDM data back to TSM\n- Updated theory of operations with SPDM session metadata handling\n\n### Reviewed Changes\n\nCopilot reviewed 2 out of 2 changed files in this pull request and generated 3 comments.\n\n| File | Description |\n| ---- | ----------- |\n| src/09-coveio_abi.adoc | Defines SPDMData structure and adds SPDM parameters to connect_device function, plus new spdm_data function |\n| src/07-theory_operations.adoc | Adds SPDM session metadata section and fixes minor grammatical errors |\n\n\n\n\n\n---\n\n<sub>**Tip:** Customize your code reviews with copilot-instructions.md. <a href=\"/riscv-non-isa/riscv-ap-tee-io/new/main/.github?filename=copilot-instructions.md\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Create the file</a> or <a href=\"https://docs.github.com/en/copilot/customizing-copilot/adding-repository-custom-instructions-for-github-copilot\" class=\"Link--inTextBlock\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">learn how to get started</a>.</sub>",
